<title>SINGAPORE: Tiger Medicals '96 net profit down 14 pct.</title>
<headline>Tiger Medicals '96 net profit down 14 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>	   (in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		9.05  vs   10.48</p>
<p>    Dividend (pct)	 20.00  vs   20.00</p>
<p>    Group share (cts)    12.00  vs   14.00</p>
<p>    Turnover		 63.96  vs   67.82</p>
<p>    Other income	    2.02  vs    1.80</p>
<p>    Interest expense	0.53  vs    0.35</p>
<p>    Pretax		   12.93  vs   14.90</p>
<p>    Tax			 3.41  vs    3.87</p>
<p>    Minorities	     (0.48) vs   (0.55)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries	 0.49  vs    nil</p>
<p>Note - Tiger Medicals Ltd, a unit of Haw Par Brothers International Ltd, said profit was down because new plants in Indonesia and Xiamen incurred further losses. Turnover was down due to the divestment of a Shanghai unit.</p>
<p>- Singapore Newsroom 65-8708080</p>
</text>
